## Unified AI core (RabbitMQ and Chat API)

Both ingress channels converge on the **same ResiRoo AI pipeline**:

1. `POST /chat/api/chat`
2. `prepare_chat_data()` in [`services/roo/app/api/services/resiroo_preparation.py`](../../../services/roo/app/api/services/resiroo_preparation.py)
3. Same prompts, context, WO lookup, image analysis, and LLM engine

**RabbitMQ path:** `ChatMessageHandler` delegates to the chat API internally (`_make_chat_api_request`).

### Ingress parity (what differs)

| Area | RabbitMQ | Chat API |
|------|----------|----------|
| **Transport** | MP queue → `message_buffer` → debounce → `resirooQueue` → handler → chat API | Direct `POST /chat/api/chat` |
| **Wait time** | Debounce window + LLM (~1–6 min typical) | Immediate (no debounce) |
| **`source`** | Always `RabbitMQ` | Use `Test` or `API` for E2E (not `RabbitMQ` unless intentionally matching production key) |
| **Conversation key** | `user_id\|session\|resident\|RabbitMQ` | `user_id\|session\|resident\|{source}` — **different thread if source differs** |
| **Auth** | Token middleware skipped when `source=RabbitMQ` | Bearer required in `meta_data.auth_bearer` or `Authorization` header |
| **`meta_data`** | Full MP `AdditionalData` from `MessageJObject` | Caller supplies MP-style keys (`ImageUrls`, `ResidentUserId`, `LocationTimeZone`, …) |
| **Outbound** | MP `MessageJObject` envelope + `TimelineSummary` to producer queue | `Result` JSON; no MP outbound queue |
| **Batching** | Multiple messages merged with `\n===\n` | One HTTP request = one turn |

**E2E rule:** Do **not** pre-fill `context_info` on chat API requests — that skips the full `prepare_chat_data()` pipeline (same as production ResiRoo).

