## Environment variables

### `VENDOROO_BASE_API_URL` (MP API switch)

| Mode | Value (Roo / roo-worker in Compose) |
|------|-------------------------------------|
| **Live MP Testing** | `https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai` |
| **Mock (`mp_mock` in Compose)** | `http://mp-mock:8099` |
| **Mock on host, Roo in Docker** | `http://host.docker.internal:8099` |
| **Both on host** | `http://127.0.0.1:8099` |

Also keep **`VENDOROO_ADMIN_AUTH_BEARER`** non-empty (mock ignores validation).

**Do not edit `.env`** for mock mode. Use **`make mp-mock-e2e-up`** (applies [`mp_mock/docker-compose.smoke.yml`](../../../mp_mock/docker-compose.smoke.yml) so `roo` / `roo-worker` get `VENDOROO_BASE_API_URL=http://mp-mock:8099`). After mock runs, restore live MP with **`make mp-mock-e2e-off`**.

**Shared infra note:** `make mp-mock-e2e-up` is the same target PMRoo uses — always run **`make mp-mock-e2e-off`** when finished so local `roo` is not left on mock for unrelated sessions.

### Other

| Variable | Notes |
|----------|--------|
| `ROO_HOST` | **`roo`** on `roo-worker` (not `localhost`) |
| `RABBITMQ_CONSUMER_QUEUE` | Inbound debounce queue (e.g. `aiAgentQueue`) |
| `RESIROO_QUEUE` | Batched handler queue (e.g. `resirooQueue`) |
| `RESIROO_DEBOUNCE_WINDOW_MINUTES` | Often 1–5 locally |

