## Post-E2E handoff (optional — after final report)

Run **only after** the E2E report is written under **`cursor_workspace/ai_test/e2e/`** per `.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/insight/y-ins-e2e-report.mdc`. Do **not** skip the report to jump straight to Slack or Jira.

### When this applies

- E2E was run for a **Jira task** that has (or will have) a **Task PR** on GitHub.
- The user is finishing the test pass and may want reviewers notified or the ticket moved to **In Review**.

If there is **no PR yet**, mention `.cursor/y-rules/git/y-y-git-create-pr.mdc` (Task PR → **`testing`**) before Slack — Slack requires an open PR URL.

---

### Step P1 — Slack PR ready for review (mandatory AskQuestion)

Before any Slack work, use **`AskQuestion`**:

| Option | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **Send Slack** | Follow `.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/slack/y-slack-pr-ready-for-review.mdc` end-to-end for this PR |
| **Skip** | Do not send Slack in this flow (default when user declines or Slack MCP unavailable) |
| **`other`** | User wants copy-paste-only template, a different channel, or to defer |

In the prompt, show the **PR number and URL** from **`gh pr view`** (current branch or user-supplied). If no PR exists, say so and offer to open one via **y-git-create-pr** first.

**When the user chooses Send Slack:**

1. Read and follow **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/slack/y-slack-pr-ready-for-review.mdc`** — do **not** shorten or skip its gates (Google Calendar prerequisite when applicable, mandatory confirmation gate, full message draft).
2. Resolve PR details with **`gh pr view <n> --json url,title,body,reviewRequests,assignees`**.
3. **Default destination:** **`#generative-search-team`** unless the user overrides in that rule.
4. Send with **`slack_send_message`** only after all confirmations in the Slack rule.
5. If Slack MCP is unavailable, offer the filled template in a fenced code block for manual paste — still confirm summary, mentions, and PR link before output.

**When the user chooses Skip:** proceed to [Step P2 — Jira In Review](#step-p2--jira-in-review-mandatory-askquestion) if applicable; do not send Slack.

---

### Step P2 — Jira In Review (mandatory AskQuestion)

**Do not** transition Jira automatically after E2E or after writing the report.

| Path | When to ask | Rule |
|------|-------------|------|
| **After successful Slack send** | Required | Use the Slack rule's **Post-send Jira confirmation** — *"Do you want me to move this Jira task to Review now?"* (**Yes** / **No**). Transition **only** on **Yes**. |
| **Slack skipped** | After P1 **Skip** (or no PR for Slack) | Use **`AskQuestion`**: *"Move this Jira task to In Review now?"* (**Yes** / **No**). Transition **only** on **Yes**. |

**On either path, when the user answers Yes:** run [Step P2a — Jira required fields](#step-p2a--jira-required-fields-before-transition) **before** calling **`transitionJiraIssue`**.

---

### Step P2a — Jira required fields (before transition)

Follow **Jira required fields before In Review (see `.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/slack/y-slack-pr-ready-for-review.mdc`)** in **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/slack/y-slack-pr-ready-for-review.mdc`** — same checklist and re-check loop for **all** In Review transitions from E2E handoff.

**Summary — all ten fields must be filled before transition:**

| Field |
|-------|
| Assignee |
| Product Owner |
| Release Coverage |
| Labels |
| Priority |
| Quality Owner |
| Sprint |
| Story Point estimate |
| Fix versions |
| Reporter |

**Workflow:**

1. **`getJiraIssue`** → show **Filled ✅ / Missing ❌** table for every field above.
2. If **any Missing ❌** → list gaps, ask user to fill in Jira, **`AskQuestion`**: **I've filled them — re-check** / **Cancel**. **Do not** transition until re-check passes.
3. When **all Filled ✅** → **`getTransitionsForJiraIssue`** → **`transitionJiraIssue`** to **In Review**.

**When user says No** (at the initial In Review question): leave Jira status unchanged — skip P2a.

**Linking E2E to Jira:** Posting test results as a Jira comment is separate — see `.cursor/rules/qa-jira-sync.mdc` when the user asks to sync QA results. Filling required Jira fields is **still mandatory** before In Review even if a QA comment was posted.

---

### Post-E2E handoff — what not to do

- Do **not** send Slack before the E2E report exists (unless the user explicitly overrides).
- Do **not** auto-send Slack or auto-transition Jira without **`AskQuestion`** confirmation.
- Do **not** move Jira to **In Review** before the user's explicit **Yes** (whether asked from the Slack rule or Step P2).
- Do **not** transition Jira without running **Step P2a** / **Jira required fields before In Review (see `.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/slack/y-slack-pr-ready-for-review.mdc`)** (re-fetch after user fills gaps).
- Do **not** include the **calendar reminder sentence** in Slack unless the user confirmed the PR review meeting is on Google Calendar (per **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/slack/y-slack-pr-ready-for-review.mdc`**).
- Do **not** invent PR URLs or Jira keys — resolve from **`gh pr view`** and branch/report metadata.

